      <body>
         <head>Punky Dunk and the Mouse</head>
         <author>Anonymous</author>
         <p rend="color(#000000)">{{GUTENBERG_LICENSE}}</p>
         <p rend="start color(#000000)">en-gutenberg-odts/a/Anonymous-PunkyDunkAndTheMouse_2006.odt</p>
         <p>Cover</p>
         <head>PUNKY DUNK AND THE MOUSE</head>
         <pb/>
         <div type="div1">
            <head>Punky Dunk and the Mouse</head>
            <pb/>
            <div type="div2">
               <head>THIS LITTLE STORY IS TOLD<lb/>AND THE LITTLE PICTURES<lb/>WERE DRAWN FOR A GOOD<lb/>LITTLE CHILD NAMED<lb/>
                  <lb/>----------------------</head>
               <lg>
                  <l>Published in the Shop of</l>
                  <l>P.F.VOLLAND &amp; CO.</l>
                  <l>CHICAGO</l>
                  <l/>
                  <l>COPYRIGHT, 1912,</l>
                  <l>P. F. VOLLAND &amp; CO.,</l>
                  <l>CHICAGO, U. S. A.</l>
                  <l>ALL RIGHTS RESERVED</l>
               </lg>
               <p rend="justify">frontis</p>
               <p rend="justify">Verse 1</p>
               <table rend="frame" xml:id="Table1">
                  <row>
                     <cell>Punky Dunk, very sly, with a wink of his eye</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>Strolled lazily all through the house;</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>To the cellar he went and the morning he spent</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>On a hunt for a fat little mouse.</cell>
                  </row>
               </table>
               <p rend="justify">Verse 2</p>
               <table rend="frame" xml:id="Table2">
                  <row>
                     <cell>"Over there by the coal," he said, "Mouse has his hole,</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>So I'll sit there beside it and wait.</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>There's a trap with some cheese just as nice as you please,</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>And Mouse soon will come out for that bait."</cell>
                  </row>
               </table>
               <p rend="justify">Verse 3</p>
               <table rend="frame" xml:id="Table3">
                  <row>
                     <cell>Punky sat by the trap, and seemed taking a nap,</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>But you know that bold Punky was wise.</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>Though he looked half asleep he was taking a peep</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>For the gleam of two bright little eyes.</cell>
                  </row>
               </table>
               <p rend="justify">Verse 4</p>
               <table rend="frame" xml:id="Table4">
                  <row>
                     <cell>Soon the mouse crept right out and went running about;</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>Punky smiled to himself and he said:</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>"I will just let him play in his own foolish way</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>Till I think that I need to be fed."</cell>
                  </row>
               </table>
               <p rend="justify">Verse 5</p>
               <table rend="frame" xml:id="Table5">
                  <row>
                     <cell>But the Mouse, too, was smart, and he got a good, start,</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>Then he leaped, and he saved his wee hide,</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>For he dashed in a hole that was not near the coal</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>But was hidden away at one side.</cell>
                  </row>
               </table>
               <table rend="frame" xml:id="Table6">
                  <row>
                     <cell>"Ha, Ha!" Punky said as he shook his white head.</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>"Well, Mouse, you may run if you please,</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>But I'll eat just the same—'twas for that that I came."</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>So he reached in the trap for the cheese.</cell>
                  </row>
               </table>
               <p rend="justify">Verse 6</p>
               <p rend="justify">Verse 7</p>
               <table rend="frame" xml:id="Table7">
                  <row>
                     <cell>Snip-snap! went the trap— Wasn't that a mishap!</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>Punky's black little paw was inside.</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>He leaped and he jumped and he ran and he bumped—</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>And the Mouse sat and laughed till he cried.</cell>
                  </row>
               </table>
               <table rend="frame" xml:id="Table8">
                  <row>
                     <cell>Punky ran up the stairs and he knocked over chairs</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>And he sprang to the table and dropped,</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>He "Meowed!" in his fright, for the trap held him tight,</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>And it was a long time till he stopped.</cell>
                  </row>
               </table>
               <p rend="justify">Verse 8</p>
               <p rend="justify">Verse 9</p>
               <table rend="frame" xml:id="Table9">
                  <row>
                     <cell>Baby's mama then came and she said: "What a shame!"</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>And she took off the trap from his paw,</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>And she wrapped it in silk and she fed him with milk</cell>
                  </row>
                  <row>
                     <cell>And she gave him some fish bones to gnaw.</cell>
                  </row>
               </table>
            </div>
         </div>
      </body>
